            <ArticleTitle>Bilateral sciatic and femoral neuropathies, rhabdomyolysis, and acute renal failure caused by positioning during radical retropubic prostatectomy.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1747-8, table of contents</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>In the hyperlordotic position, the patient's hips are above the feet and head. We present a case of rhabdomyolysis, acute renal failure, and bilateral femoral and sciatic neuropathies caused by this position.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
